00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:50.480
businesses and stuff like that maybe off of Route 6.

00:31:51.440 --> 00:31:55.120
I just know I don't want to be in this position again next year

00:31:55.695 --> 00:31:57.935
having to look

00:31:57.935 --> 00:32:01.215
into where the budget is and all that. Thank you.

00:32:04.335 --> 00:32:05.535
Thanks Eric.

00:32:06.895 --> 00:32:07.855
Ryan Werner.

00:32:09.900 --> 00:32:23.725
>> I know I've said pretty much hit everything on the head, but I just want to make sure that when you're budgeting for AES that you make sure that you're meeting all the AES contractual needs and that you're fully funding what was mutually negotiated between the teachers union and the town,

00:32:24.285 --> 00:32:27.005
and that you're not going to short fund them. You.

00:32:32.925 --> 00:32:33.965
Thanks Ryan.

00:32:35.485 --> 00:32:36.445
Jennifer Thompson.

00:32:42.660 --> 00:32:44.180
Nothing for me. Thank you.

00:32:45.860 --> 00:32:48.260
Thank you. Elizabeth Partridge.

00:32:50.835 --> 00:32:51.715
>> Yes.

00:32:51.875 --> 00:32:54.115
So I have a couple of different issues,

00:32:54.915 --> 00:32:57.635
and mostly from things that people have already said.

00:32:59.795 --> 00:33:01.955
One individual said that we're

00:33:01.955 --> 00:33:04.995
doing such a good job that we're drawing parents,

00:33:04.995 --> 00:33:07.510
but it certainly doesn't show that in the enrollment.

00:33:07.990 --> 00:33:09.510
I did speak to someone

00:33:10.150 --> 00:33:19.350
who was in contact with the State Board of Education regarding the optimal class size. And the State Board of Education told them that the optimal class size is between eighteen and nineteen.

00:33:19.995 --> 00:33:20.635
And

00:33:20.955 --> 00:33:23.595
so, think that we're well below that in most cases.

00:33:24.155 --> 00:33:42.870
One problem with the small class size is the concept of being the odd man out. Imagine that you have 10 kids in your class, five boys, five girls, four of these girls get along well, and you're the fifth girl who's the odd man out. It's a lot harder for a kid who just doesn't fit in to stick out in that kind of situation.

00:33:43.430 --> 00:33:53.085
Someone had said something about this is a different world than what we grew up in. Apparently, it's not a different world in Bolton where the average class size of fourth graders is

00:33:53.485 --> 00:33:57.085
19 and the average class size of first graders is 20.

00:33:57.645 --> 00:34:00.765
In Marlborough, the average class size across the entire

00:34:01.720 --> 00:34:04.280
elementary school is 22. In Hebron,

00:34:04.840 --> 00:34:09.000
the first graders average 18 and the fourth grades average 19.

00:34:09.080 --> 00:34:10.200
In Columbia,

00:34:10.360 --> 00:34:13.320
the first graders are 15 and the fourth graders are 23.

00:34:13.805 --> 00:34:20.525
So, apparently it's a different world in Andover, but not a different world in other places around here. I do have to agree with Marci.

00:34:20.525 --> 00:34:25.485
It does seem that there's an awful lot of bullying going on, and that really is unacceptable.

00:34:26.045 --> 00:34:31.500
I also think that using children a pawn within these meetings is unacceptable.

00:34:32.220 --> 00:34:36.780
We're there at these meetings to learn and to listen. And when we can't do that,

00:34:37.660 --> 00:34:40.860
it takes away from the meeting. And it's no different than if we had

00:34:42.615 --> 00:34:48.535
a protest outside their school. They're in their classroom trying to learn just like this is our classroom and we're trying to learn.

00:34:49.415 --> 00:34:58.910
The other thing about class sizes, I've spoken to two different teachers at Ram Middle School who say that the Andover students actually struggle because the class size is larger at Ram.

00:34:59.230 --> 00:34:59.710
So,

00:35:01.390 --> 00:35:16.195
are a lot of things going on here. And I think it's time, as Eric just said, it's time for us to start looking at, can we regionalize? Is there a way? If we have to have larger class time, can we regionalize and get a half time person in some of these other situations,

00:35:16.355 --> 00:35:17.875
the specialists that we need?

00:35:20.355 --> 00:35:33.930
We've got to find a middle ground. And what's happening is there's a group of people who are voting this budget down because they think it's too high, and there's another group that's voting it down because they think it's too low. And somewhere along the line, we need to find a middle ground.

00:35:37.450 --> 00:35:38.410
>> Thank you.

00:35:39.975 --> 00:35:41.095
Caitlin McIntosh.

00:35:55.000 --> 00:35:58.760
All right, we'll circle back around. Next up, Dave Kwazewski.

